A||||27||Indiana_resto_guy||Somebody flamming Fierodave? ||||1||
Z||000000||Indiana_resto_guy||06-10-2001||04:27 PM||||This is from the mall posting by 86seyellow:<P>(The spelling and grammar have been left unchanged in the original posting by choice!)<P>   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 86seyellow:<BR><B>FieroDave: <P>Seems you always have something for sale. I wonder if everyone knows you steal all of these cars cheap, part what you want and resell to other fiero owners at triple the price. We are all here to help keep fieros on the road. I ahve no prob with making money but you seem to be a con man. I have severla cases from other fiero board members on here. Get some class ok<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>       <BR> Profile for 86seyellow  <P>Date Registered: 05-01-2001  <BR>Status: Member  <BR>Total Posts: 18  <BR>Current Email: ace101@hotmail.com  <BR>Homepage: http://  <BR>Occupation: fiero test driver  <BR>Location: wabasha, Minnesota, 55981  <BR>Interests: fiero, speed, girls  <BR>ICQ Number:    <BR> <BR>SO . . . lets talk about CLASS!<BR>86seyellow apparently has none! I'm just wondering how a NEW member with less than 45 days of being on the Forum can really start flaming ANYONE in that amount of time.<BR>As you can guess by my member name(86seyellow), I restore these cars. I have done, (and will continue to do so), business with FIERODAVE on a fairly regular basis and have bought several cars from him. Here's a list for information (with prices if anyone cares)<BR>'88 GT T-Top car with 44K from CA and rust free, $2800.00<BR>'88 Formula with 160K from CA and rust free, $1000.00<BR>'88 Coupe with 77K from CA and rust free,$400.00<BR>There is another coupe out there if I want it for shipping!<BR>'86 GT rolling chassis with 111K for $600.00<BR>and other miscellaneous parts listed on his site.<P>I know also that with the CA deal that Dave has been closing of 4 other Fieros that went to Milwaukee (all GT's) that were low miles and had comparable prices of mine!<P>I did less than 3 weeks ago sold him an '86 GT for $2000.00 which needed a new transmission. Dave came down to my house and labored over this car for 3 days using low mileage parts he had for sale on his site to repair this car. While at it, we discovered that the bottom end of the engine was ready to let loose and I installed new main and rod bearings with a new high volume oil pump.<BR>This car he has already sold to Monkeyman for I think $3400.00. Just for an example to indicate that Dave stands behind what he sells, Monkeyman developed an oil leak on his way home. Dave drove down to pick up the car(400 miles) took it back to his house, repaired the leak (oil sending unit) and THEN delivered it to Monkeyman (in Indiana) for the price of fuel! Now if I wanted to sit down and do the math on the deal I think that I would find that Dave came very close to breaking even on that deal, if he didn't loose $$$!<BR>Just who is it that's getting ripped off?<P>So about getting some CLASS I wonder who it is that needs to get some? (86seyellow) you might check Fierodave's site, he may have some for sale!<BR>My thought's are that before you start slamming some one, get your facts straight and ducks in a row FIRST!<P>Anyone else?<P>Oh, the '87 SE T-Top car is sold! I have already purchased it!<p>[This message has been edited by Indiana_resto_guy (edited 06-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Galen||06-10-2001||04:31 PM||||get the ducks..<P>FieroDave has always seemed classy to me, though I haven't bought anything from him personally, I have heard numerous good things about him. If I wasn't a poor southern boy I prolly would buy some stuff from em.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Rock on Mr Resto  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Galen - 1988 Hawaiian Orchid Coupe Auto 4Banger - <A HREF="http://myfiero.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero Website</A><BR>AIM: WookieeNC||||reg||1
Z||000002||cadaver||06-10-2001||04:56 PM||||So when a wreaking yard get a car for $100 then charges for the parts you take is that any different.<P>I have done alot of business with FIERODAVE and have never found him to be anything but honorable. His prices are reasonable.<BR>I would do business with him again.<BR>As for you I would have to think hard about that one. Even when he hard our differences he was still a stand up guy.<P>Keep it up Dave||||reg||1
