Z||000005||Oreif||06-10-2001||06:37 PM||||Didn't FieroDave buy a large lot full of cars and parts? I thought the money was 6 figures or close to it. So I wouldn't say he stole the cars as cheap. But 86seyellow wasn't even a member of the forum last fall when FieroDave bought all those parts. The prices he's charging are about average on some and less than average on most. Hell a junk yard will pay $25 to $50 for a car around here and make over $5000 in parts then crush the remains and make money on the scrap. As for FieroDave's parts, I think the quality and prices are good.||||reg||1
Z||000006||wahoo4u||06-10-2001||06:51 PM||||just to put in my two cents worth.  I have just recently met fiero dave and purchased a low milage engine, cradle and all, from his CA adventure.  The engine is now in the car and runs beautifully.  A new engine alone would have cost me more than what i paid for my whole set up in the car.  I had no problems with dave and he went more than out of his way to see that i got what i wanted.  Thanks again dave.  Hope to see you again soon with a running fiero.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||fropuff||06-10-2001||07:10 PM||||I feel bad that we live in the same friggin state!  If you ever bought anything from Dave, which I'm sure you haven't, you would know that the stuff he sells is top notch.  I've gotten some things from him, and everything goes great.  We did a little trade for my tail lens.  He got the tail lens with a busted cover, and I got seat belt holders (that he colored gray to match my interior--turned out great!), as well as a free shifter knob to boot!  Whenever I've emailed him, it's been a matter of hours until I hear a reply.  I wanted a marker lens, he told me to go elsewhere!  He said it would be cheaper.  I wanted a drip rail, he told me to go to a dealer to save me some shipping!  How's that for a good guy?  He actually told me to get the parts another place to save me money!  I won't hesitate ever again to get parts from him.  If you'd look at all his feedback on eBay, all of it's good!  There's hundreds of happy customers!  Now, how about you name the people that are talkin $hit about him?  Oh yeah...get some class!||||reg||1
Z||000008||Fierochic88||06-10-2001||08:33 PM||||Not only do you get good parts from FieroDave, you also get a 24-7 help hotline.  I bought a headliner off of him for my ex's car and he enclosed wonderful installation instructions and his home phone in case we needed any more assistance.  Plus my dad just got rims off him and they are just what he asked for, plus Dave sold them to him at a good price!<P>Jennifer<BR>Silver 88 GT<BR>Silver 87 Cp<BR>Cobalt Blue 85 GT||||reg||1
Z||000009||maryjane||06-10-2001||08:58 PM||||A perspective from a fairly new member:<BR>I might make a joke or too, but all in fun. Haven't personally met any of you but have received a lot of help and replies from many including fierodave. As far as flaming goes, I avoid posting to these threads if possible,<BR>mostly because they're just none of my d*** business! <BR>Don||||reg||1
Z||000010||fiero56||06-10-2001||09:07 PM||||<B>But 86seyellow wasn't even a member of the forum last fall when FieroDave bought all those parts. </B><P>I've said it before, and ignorance is no exuse. This forum has been gaining a few members in the dipshit category, and I think 86seyellow fits nicely. There are some people who really need to grow up.||||reg||1
Z||000011||AusFiero||06-10-2001||09:20 PM||||Well from reading good prices on Daves stuff myself and obviously good service what is SE on about. SE how old are you? Do you understand business? <P>See in business the idea is to buy or manufacture items, then calculate your selling price based on: the initial capital and time outlayed, a cut for the tax man, a loading for keeping it in stock (storage space isn't free in business even if it is a garage), a fair rate for your time in processing the items from when they come in to when they go out and then you have to put a profit margin on it to keep a roof over your head and feed the wife and kids. <P>That is just some of the variables and I could go in with warranty coverage, stock insurance, etc etc etc. <P>Get a life SE! Wow my first flame, small as it may be  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/fiero5.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>Need a Subwoofer Console or Speaker Door Pods?||||reg||1
Z||000012||DJRice||06-10-2001||09:48 PM||||Not to mention the fact that I think twice now Dave has held Forum contests and given a prize to the winner.  I won a wing from him last summer.  <P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/djr_signature.jpg"> ||||reg||1
